Package: jstats
Title: Simplified Statistical Analysis Tools for Social Science
Version: 0.9.154
Authors@R:
    person("Jeff", "Ackerman", , "SurveyCentre@griffith.edu.au", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides simplified tools for common statistical analyses
    used in social science research and teaching, with output formatted
    in the style of 'SPSS', 'Stata', or 'SAS'. Analysis functions include
    descriptive statistics, frequency tables, t-tests, ANOVA,
    correlations, chi-square tests, cross-tabulations, linear regression,
    logistic regression, and Cronbach's alpha, with built-in model
    diagnostics and plotting. Supporting tools handle data management
    (recoding, labelling, encoding text as coded values, case selection,
    dummy coding, scale construction, data screening) and unified data
    import and export for 'SPSS', 'Stata', 'SAS', 'Excel', CSV, and R
    formats. Declared missing values are read and written faithfully in
    each platform's own convention, can be declared or converted between
    conventions within R, and suspected but undeclared missing-value
    codes are detected automatically. Functions accept unquoted variable
    names and formula syntax, handle 'haven'-labelled variables directly,
    and return results invisibly while printing readable tables. The
    package stays close enough to base R conventions that users learn
    transferable skills rather than a private dialect, easing the
    transition from 'SPSS', 'Stata', or 'SAS' into the broader R
    ecosystem.
